{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Endpoint responses can hide distinct intermediate networks. For an explicitly supplied finite linear network and calibrated change to one connection, this note derives a necessary relation across three full responses, a deterministic error bound, and the first changed impulse-response order. A positive-spring chain and triangle have the same original boundary response but differ under the same physically identified intervention.\n\nThe result is `bounded_theorem` / `conditional-support`, with `upstream_support` trace to a future fixed-action scalar/environment response. The action, physical coordinates, preparation, source/readout, intervention calibration and measured scales remain supplied conditions. This is established matrix/projection mathematics made into a conditional discriminator; it does not derive quantum probabilities or validate an underlying physical network. No empirical data enter this PR.\n\n[Self-contained note](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/docs/LOCAL_NETWORK_INTERVENTION_RESPONSE_NOTE_2026-10-16.md), [primary runner](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/scripts/local_network_response.py), [imported helper](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/scripts/local_network_response_math.py), [canonical cache](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/logs/runner-cache/local_network_response.txt).\n\n[Handoff](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/.claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/HANDOFF.md), [trace gate](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/.claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/TRACE_GATE.md), [assumptions and imports](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/.claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/ASSUMPTIONS_AND_IMPORTS.md), [section-by-section review preparation](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/.claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/REVIEW_HISTORY.md).\n\nValidation: the primary completes14controlfamilies with a fresh120-second source/input-bound cache. Thirteen deliberate scratch mutations fail their intended sign, coefficient, order, degeneracy or error-bound assertions; the final-note-bound batch is [preserved here](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/outputs/local_network_response/mutation_repeat_v2/mutation_controls_v1.json). The [focused independent check](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/outputs/local_network_response/independent/REPORT.md) completes64assertions and reproduces the14primarycontrols exactly; counts overlap and are not summed as independent tests. [Mutation addendum](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/outputs/local_network_response/independent/MUTATION_ADDENDUM.md) and [metadata check](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/outputs/local_network_response/independent/METADATA_ADDENDUM.md) bind final sources and claims.\n\nReproduce with `python3 scripts/local_network_response.py` (or `--json`). Python compilation, JSON parsing, vocabulary, source/evidence hashes and complete base-to-head whitespace checks pass. The citation-manifest delta acknowledges exactly one new zero-edge note node; its helper is discovered through the ordinary import. [Focused preflight](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/e97535fef2ce2da544c288fe81a7cb35a0d8914b/outputs/local_network_response/focused_preflight_v1.json) records the scope.\n\nThis standalone95-file delta is based directly on main `bbada1fe09b2d10d610560864d86b68c24a59713`; it has no unmerged science dependency. Most files preserve execution/check evidence. Shared integrated-main pipeline, strict audit lint and changed-evidence landing gates remain pending. Independent audit is still required for any effective retained status. No merge or audit verdict is requested or applied.\n","files":[{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/APPROACH_REGISTRY.md","additions":11,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/ARTIFACT_PLAN.md","additions":8,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/ASSUMPTIONS_AND_IMPORTS.md","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE.md","additions":5,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/GOAL.md","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/HANDOFF.md","additions":9,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/LITERATURE_BRIDGES.md","additions":5,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/NO_GO_LEDGER.md","additions":3,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/OPPORTUNITY_QUEUE.md","additions":7,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/neighborhood-intervention-response-20261016/REVIEW_HI